ttle bit but the  good news is that this can be fixed as  well with bandage joint distractions so  what we're going to do here is wrap a  band around the foot  let's get the shoe off again  between where the bridge of the foot  meets  the bottom of the shin  which is called the talus and we're  going to try and pull it back and down  this is basically going to pull the  phibia back into alignment so that we  can bend our foot upwards again your  pocket band  find an anchor point  that could be a table leg a heavy table  leg i'm actually going to use a  kettlebell here which is fine because i  just need to use my other foot to keep  that in place and i'm also going to use  my other foot to pin the band downwards  to keep that angle  how i want it  so i put my foot on the kettlebell  and see it's across  where the bridge of the foot meets the  tibia and the fibula  pulling down  on that tailless bone  now i'm just going to bend nice and  forward  as you're doing this you should  immediately  find that you can  lean your foot forwards more than you  could before hold this position for 5 to  10 seconds repeat 15 times and you  should find that you immediately  following this have a deeper squat and  feel less discomfort when you get into  that position this helped me immediately  to increase my range of motion and to  ease off some of the ankle pain i've  experienced in the past  hopefully it could do the same for some  of you  two great sources for more on those  specific joint distractions are scott  university and athlete next check them  out if you want more advice like that so  thanks so much for watching this one  guys i hope you found it useful and  interesting if you did then please  consider liking sharing it around that  would help me out immensely subscribe if  you want to see more like this hit the  bell button for notifications and if you  like this kind of training that improves  your general performance working on not  only strength and balance balls mobi